From 3304c4163a8edd4ae1c32400b44b0efe5dd80774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:40:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebrand to H.E.M. - Hammarberg Energy Manager; fix stale
 upstream report-problem/docs links
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Håkan (2026-10-03): rename the app from the inconsistent BESS/BESS Manager/
Home Energy Manager/Battery Manager mix to one name everywhere: H.E.M. -
Hammarberg Energy Manager. Full name in primary titles (dashboard header
via a short H.E.M. + expanding subtitle, add-on name, browser tab title,
DOCS.md, docs/agents/bess-knowledge.md); short H.E.M. in constrained UI
space and running prose (alert banners, AI chat panel, settings subtitle,
setup wizard, debug export headers, AI analyst system prompt/tool
descriptions). panel_title kept as the short form only - HA's sidebar has
little room for a long add-on title. core/bess/* module paths, the
core.bess Python package, and the bess:demo-mode-changed internal DOM
event name are untouched - internal plumbing, not the displayed brand.
config.yaml bumped to v0.1.18.

Also fixed two stale leftovers from the upstream fork, found while editing
these exact files: 'Report a Problem' built its GitHub issue URL against
upstream's own repo (johanzander/bess-manager) instead of this fork
(hakanhammarberg-hue/home_energy_manager), so a real bug report would have
gone nowhere Håkan could see it; and DOCS.md's InfluxDB config example
still showed the old v1 username/password schema instead of the real v2
org/bucket/token schema this app actually uses.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, npm run build green (2756 modules, same as
before), full frontend vitest suite 130/130 green, backend pytest 71/71
green.
